(1526599, 202064, 25397, '<td valign="top">It''s difficult to expose correctly in bright sunlight, especially if you have a point-and-shoot like me. I''d recommend first focussing/metering on the brightest part of the scene you are taking and then moving the camera into position while holding down the button. This way less will turn out over exposed and you can simply brighten with levels or curves.</td>', 'It''s difficult to expose correctly in bright sunlight, especially if you have a point-and-shoot like me. I''d recommend first focussing/metering on the brightest part of the scene you are taking and then moving the camera into position while holding down the button. This way less will turn out over exposed and you can simply brighten with levels or curves.', '2005-07-11 12:53:38.000000', NULL, 1),
