(1536238, 202447, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 1/2<br/>Photo Quality: 0/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 0/2<br/> <br/>The post processing hurts your image. There should have been more initial lighting to avoid the blown out areas around the table lamp. The image is very grainy.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 1/2Color/Contrast: 1/2Photo Quality: 0/2Composition: 2/2My Subjective Affinity: 0/2 The post processing hurts your image. There should have been more initial lighting to avoid the blown out areas around the table lamp. The image is very grainy.', '2005-07-14 19:42:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1536242, 202256, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 1/2<br/>Photo Quality: 1/2<br/>Composition: 2/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2<br/> <br/>The cropping of the image was done nicely. Father and child out participating in an activity together really brings out the family meaning. The father is too dark and the image is not the sharpest. The sky is very hazy.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 2/2Color/Contrast: 1/2Photo Quality: 1/2Composition: 2/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2 The cropping of the image was done nicely. Father and child out participating in an activity together really brings out the family meaning. The father is too dark and the image is not the sharpest. The sky is very hazy.', '2005-07-14 19:44:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1536247, 201320, 39144, '<td valign="top">Fit Challenge Criteria: 0/2<br/>Color/Contrast: 2/2<br/>Photo Quality: 2/2<br/>Composition: 1/2<br/>My Subjective Affinity: 1/2<br/> <br/>The photo is very well exposed. However, the cropping on the left side is too tight to make the best use of the rule of thirds.</td>', 'Fit Challenge Criteria: 0/2Color/Contrast: 2/2Photo Quality: 2/2Composition: 1/2My Subjective Affinity: 1/2 The photo is very well exposed. However, the cropping on the left side is too tight to make the best use of the rule of thirds.', '2005-07-14 19:46:25.000000', NULL, 1),
