(1539893, 202498, 4793, '<td valign="top">Beautiful baby</td>', 'Beautiful baby', '2005-07-16 23:17:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1539902, 201773, 4793, '<td valign="top">Excellente colors, your composition is perfect, reflections great, the swans are bit overexposed.</td>', 'Excellente colors, your composition is perfect, reflections great, the swans are bit overexposed.', '2005-07-16 23:21:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540004, 202345, 10261, '<td valign="top">The DOF seems to have been centered on the flora in the background. Because the boy is not uniformly blurry, some or all of the soft focus may have been due to motion blur. If this is the case, a faster shutter speed would have helped.<br/></td>', 'The DOF seems to have been centered on the flora in the background. Because the boy is not uniformly blurry, some or all of the soft focus may have been due to motion blur. If this is the case, a faster shutter speed would have helped.', '2005-07-17 00:20:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540010, 200964, 25397, '<td valign="top">A little brightness/ contrast adjustments could improve this photo</td>', 'A little brightness/ contrast adjustments could improve this photo', '2005-07-17 00:23:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540019, 202488, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very cute!</td>', 'Very cute!', '2005-07-17 00:27:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540020, 202469, 10261, '<td valign="top">As presented here, this image seems to have crossed the border between high-key and overexposed. Since there is still a fair amount of shadow detail, I suspect that you could bring back a lot of the tonal range by setting your white/black points and reducing the contrast. The harsh shadow cast by the guy''s profile suggests that this scene was primarily lit by a single bright light just above the camera. If you intended this photo to look high-key, using a reflector to soften the edges of that shadow would have made this look more professional.</td>', 'As presented here, this image seems to have crossed the border between high-key and overexposed. Since there is still a fair amount of shadow detail, I suspect that you could bring back a lot of the tonal range by setting your white/black points and reducing the contrast. The harsh shadow cast by the guy''s profile suggests that this scene was primarily lit by a single bright light just above the camera. If you intended this photo to look high-key, using a reflector to soften the edges of that shadow would have made this look more professional.', '2005-07-17 00:28:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540024, 202404, 25397, '<td valign="top">The gravestone seems a bit old for the youngin to be connected, but whatever, it''s a nice photo.</td>', 'The gravestone seems a bit old for the youngin to be connected, but whatever, it''s a nice photo.', '2005-07-17 00:30:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540026, 200826, 25397, '<td valign="top">Brilliant idea</td>', 'Brilliant idea', '2005-07-17 00:31:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540028, 201949, 10261, '<td valign="top">This looks underexposed and unevenly lit. The framing of the headstone feels uncomfortable. I think that you''d be better off centering the image, or placing it about a third of the way from the edge; some additional breathing room above the tombstone would be nice too. Rendering this in B&amp;W was a good choice, but the low contrast muddies the textures (which look like they might have otherwise been a strong compositional element). Adding some noise would have given this image a more nostalgic feel, which I think would have reinforced the mood.</td>', 'This looks underexposed and unevenly lit. The framing of the headstone feels uncomfortable. I think that you''d be better off centering the image, or placing it about a third of the way from the edge; some additional breathing room above the tombstone would be nice too. Rendering this in B&W was a good choice, but the low contrast muddies the textures (which look like they might have otherwise been a strong compositional element). Adding some noise would have given this image a more nostalgic feel, which I think would have reinforced the mood.', '2005-07-17 00:35:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540033, 202413, 25397, '<td valign="top">brillaint!</td>', 'brillaint!', '2005-07-17 00:37:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540035, 201690, 25397, '<td valign="top">Too studio and set up for such a shot. I mean, I don''t hate set up shots but this seems way too corney with the plain background, poses, ect. A tighter crop would have helped as well</td>', 'Too studio and set up for such a shot. I mean, I don''t hate set up shots but this seems way too corney with the plain background, poses, ect. A tighter crop would have helped as well', '2005-07-17 00:39:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540038, 202480, 10261, '<td valign="top">There is no clear point of focus in this image. The focus seems sharpest on the bright white headstone, but since it''s occluded by the larger items in the foreground it''s probably not the intended subject. A much narrower DOF and composition which clearly indicated the intended subject would have helped this image dramatically.</td>', 'There is no clear point of focus in this image. The focus seems sharpest on the bright white headstone, but since it''s occluded by the larger items in the foreground it''s probably not the intended subject. A much narrower DOF and composition which clearly indicated the intended subject would have helped this image dramatically.', '2005-07-17 00:41:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540043, 202374, 25397, '<td valign="top">I like your crop choice, pose and simplicity here.<br/>However, the whole thing seems to be a bit Neat Image abused.</td>', 'I like your crop choice, pose and simplicity here.However, the whole thing seems to be a bit Neat Image abused.', '2005-07-17 00:45:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540045, 202379, 33400, '<td valign="top">Very touching and nicely simple (if that makes sense).  good portrait</td>', 'Very touching and nicely simple (if that makes sense).  good portrait', '2005-07-17 00:47:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540046, 202470, 11800, '<td valign="top">nice processing.</td>', 'nice processing.', '2005-07-17 00:48:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540048, 202210, 15711, '<td valign="top">OK THIS DOES IT! That is the most adorable thing I have ever seen. If this doesn''t win, then I''m a complete idiot.  ON MY GOD - <br/> <br/>I just ran across this again and it is still my absolute favorite. If I could vote higher than 10,  I would.  The whole picture is just spectacular. The focus, the composition. The contrast of their little heads and ears against their bodies which just blends into the background only to be broken up by those little pink noses and feet. AUGHHHHH!!</td>', 'OK THIS DOES IT! That is the most adorable thing I have ever seen. If this doesn''t win, then I''m a complete idiot.  ON MY GOD -  I just ran across this again and it is still my absolute favorite. If I could vote higher than 10,  I would.  The whole picture is just spectacular. The focus, the composition. The contrast of their little heads and ears against their bodies which just blends into the background only to be broken up by those little pink noses and feet. AUGHHHHH!!', '2005-07-17 00:49:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540050, 201142, 33400, '<td valign="top">You can''t get more family than this.  Great focal point.</td>', 'You can''t get more family than this.  Great focal point.', '2005-07-17 00:49:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540051, 202392, 10261, '<td valign="top">The horizon doesn''t look level; see <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=21" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a> page for information on how to correct this. Because the only strong color in the image is the red street I think that the composition would have been improved by either converting this to B&amp;W or by desaturating only the street. Without the clue provided by the challenge topic I''d be hard pressed to decide whether this was a photo of the statuary which three people happened to wander into or a snapshot of a family vacation. Shooting this from a low angle with the people standing near the monument and the stone figures towering over them would have been a much stronger image.</td>', 'The horizon doesn''t look level; see this page for information on how to correct this. Because the only strong color in the image is the red street I think that the composition would have been improved by either converting this to B&W or by desaturating only the street. Without the clue provided by the challenge topic I''d be hard pressed to decide whether this was a photo of the statuary which three people happened to wander into or a snapshot of a family vacation. Shooting this from a low angle with the people standing near the monument and the stone figures towering over them would have been a much stronger image.', '2005-07-17 00:49:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540053, 202255, 11800, '<td valign="top">Like the dof.</td>', 'Like the dof.', '2005-07-17 00:50:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540054, 201842, 10261, '<td valign="top">Although a very creative photo of a family could have been made with these masks, this image doesn''t appear to demonstrate any attempt to relate them to the challenge topic.</td>', 'Although a very creative photo of a family could have been made with these masks, this image doesn''t appear to demonstrate any attempt to relate them to the challenge topic.', '2005-07-17 00:51:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540058, 201367, 10261, '<td valign="top">The focus is rather soft and seems to have been centered on the water behind the boy. A faster shutter speed or deeper DOF may have corrected this. The crop above the kid seems a bit too aggressive to me; I''d rather see a bit more headroom.</td>', 'The focus is rather soft and seems to have been centered on the water behind the boy. A faster shutter speed or deeper DOF may have corrected this. The crop above the kid seems a bit too aggressive to me; I''d rather see a bit more headroom.', '2005-07-17 00:53:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540064, 201854, 11800, '<td valign="top">Isn''t he the lucky duck. The colors are very clear.  The more I look at this, the more surreal it looks with the innocent hand placement and all.</td>', 'Isn''t he the lucky duck. The colors are very clear.  The more I look at this, the more surreal it looks with the innocent hand placement and all.', '2005-07-17 00:56:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540065, 202334, 10261, '<td valign="top">This is a cute pose and a very nice candid. On a technical note, the DOF is too shallow and brings unnecessary attention to the younger girl''s hair.</td>', 'This is a cute pose and a very nice candid. On a technical note, the DOF is too shallow and brings unnecessary attention to the younger girl''s hair.', '2005-07-17 00:56:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540092, 202249, 10261, '<td valign="top">I''d love to know where this photo was taken. I would be interested in vacationing there myself some day.<br/> <br/>The mottled light on the people in the foreground is distracting. Under the given lighting conditions I think that composing the shot so that the figures were closer to the waterfall would have produced a stronger photograph.</td>', 'I''d love to know where this photo was taken. I would be interested in vacationing there myself some day. The mottled light on the people in the foreground is distracting. Under the given lighting conditions I think that composing the shot so that the figures were closer to the waterfall would have produced a stronger photograph.', '2005-07-17 01:06:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540127, 201984, 10261, '<td valign="top">It looks like the focus on the original image may have been too soft, and you then over-sharpened to try to compensate for this. The color cast makes this look like a faded family snapshot; if this was intentional, adding a little bit of noise might have helped to flesh out the effect. It may just be the odd shape of the shore in the background, but the horizon feels like it''s tipped slightly.</td>', 'It looks like the focus on the original image may have been too soft, and you then over-sharpened to try to compensate for this. The color cast makes this look like a faded family snapshot; if this was intentional, adding a little bit of noise might have helped to flesh out the effect. It may just be the odd shape of the shore in the background, but the horizon feels like it''s tipped slightly.', '2005-07-17 01:12:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540135, 202331, 10261, '<td valign="top">The focus seems to be on the tree in the background. Since advanced editing was allowed for this challenge, cloning out the glare on the woman''s lipstick would have improved the shot.</td>', 'The focus seems to be on the tree in the background. Since advanced editing was allowed for this challenge, cloning out the glare on the woman''s lipstick would have improved the shot.', '2005-07-17 01:14:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540137, 202460, 10261, '<td valign="top">The light seems rather flat.</td>', 'The light seems rather flat.', '2005-07-17 01:15:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540153, 200982, 10261, '<td valign="top">Technically, this is a fairly good shot. However, due to the rather unsavory subject matter I rather doubt that it''s technical merits will rescue your score. Without the title I''d have had difficulty identifying the textured surface under the flys; an angle which included a fin or some other recognizable feature would have improved the composition (although it might have made the subject more unappealing).</td>', 'Technically, this is a fairly good shot. However, due to the rather unsavory subject matter I rather doubt that it''s technical merits will rescue your score. Without the title I''d have had difficulty identifying the textured surface under the flys; an angle which included a fin or some other recognizable feature would have improved the composition (although it might have made the subject more unappealing).', '2005-07-17 01:18:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540168, 202444, 10261, '<td valign="top">The focus seems sharpest on the strap for the S230. If your image wasn''t  being evaluated solely by people who will probably like to see a kid with a camera, I''d say that the photo would be stronger without it. Overall I like the shot, but I think that shooting it from a lower angle (looking up at the kid) and having a stronger catchlight would have improved the image.</td>', 'The focus seems sharpest on the strap for the S230. If your image wasn''t  being evaluated solely by people who will probably like to see a kid with a camera, I''d say that the photo would be stronger without it. Overall I like the shot, but I think that shooting it from a lower angle (looking up at the kid) and having a stronger catchlight would have improved the image.', '2005-07-17 01:24:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540183, 200770, 10261, '<td valign="top">The title seems a bit morbid. I''d have preferred a crop which allowed more breathing room.</td>', 'The title seems a bit morbid. I''d have preferred a crop which allowed more breathing room.', '2005-07-17 01:26:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540189, 201388, 10261, '<td valign="top">The desaturation doesn''t seem to add anything to the image.</td>', 'The desaturation doesn''t seem to add anything to the image.', '2005-07-17 01:28:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540192, 201602, 10261, '<td valign="top">A deeper DOF would have helped this image. The image would feel more balanced if there was more room in the direction that the kid is looking.</td>', 'A deeper DOF would have helped this image. The image would feel more balanced if there was more room in the direction that the kid is looking.', '2005-07-17 01:30:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540204, 202374, 10261, '<td valign="top">The dead space in the foreground, the lack of headroom and the fact that the woman is bending over make it feel like the frame is falling. I think that at least cropping out some of the foreground would have improved the image.</td>', 'The dead space in the foreground, the lack of headroom and the fact that the woman is bending over make it feel like the frame is falling. I think that at least cropping out some of the foreground would have improved the image.', '2005-07-17 01:33:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540207, 202328, 10261, '<td valign="top">More headroom for the statue in the foreground would have improved the composition.</td>', 'More headroom for the statue in the foreground would have improved the composition.', '2005-07-17 01:34:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540213, 202076, 10261, '<td valign="top">Nice use of DOF and selective desaturation to draw attention to the subject.</td>', 'Nice use of DOF and selective desaturation to draw attention to the subject.', '2005-07-17 01:36:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540222, 202177, 10261, '<td valign="top">A sharper focus would have improved this image. So far this is one of my favorite images of the challenge.</td>', 'A sharper focus would have improved this image. So far this is one of my favorite images of the challenge.', '2005-07-17 01:39:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540234, 202255, 10261, '<td valign="top">This is way oversharpened. Aside from that, this is one of the better ones in the challenge.</td>', 'This is way oversharpened. Aside from that, this is one of the better ones in the challenge.', '2005-07-17 01:44:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540297, 201982, 1031, '<td valign="top">Funny idea (reminds me of one I did with some trees) and great lighting.</td>', 'Funny idea (reminds me of one I did with some trees) and great lighting.', '2005-07-17 02:26:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540304, 201612, 10261, '<td valign="top">The DOF seems a bit too shallow; I''d like to see sharp focus on the boy too. I particularly like the lighting. This image suggests that an interesting story is underway and does a good job of capturing the moment. Keep up the great work, Joey!</td>', 'The DOF seems a bit too shallow; I''d like to see sharp focus on the boy too. I particularly like the lighting. This image suggests that an interesting story is underway and does a good job of capturing the moment. Keep up the great work, Joey!', '2005-07-17 02:29:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540306, 202413, 1031, '<td valign="top">Hope that didn''t happen bonking the nost on the lens : )<br/>A rare moment to capture indeed.</td>', 'Hope that didn''t happen bonking the nost on the lens : )A rare moment to capture indeed.', '2005-07-17 02:29:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1540310, 202329, 1031, '<td valign="top">I''m OK with B&amp;W for a flowery field, but I think I''d increase the contrast a little in the darker midtones.</td>', 'I''m OK with B&W for a flowery field, but I think I''d increase the contrast a little in the darker midtones.', '2005-07-17 02:32:19.000000', NULL, 1),
