(1546271, 200982, 35357, '<td valign="top">We pretty much have the same camera, only my MP are a bit higher than yours.  I''m inspired by your shot and am adding it to my favourites to remind me of what a great image can come out of this camera.  Thanks for doing such a great job on this photo and inspiring me to keep trying for shots like this just when I was starting to get down on myself and my camera.  Great job!</td>', 'We pretty much have the same camera, only my MP are a bit higher than yours.  I''m inspired by your shot and am adding it to my favourites to remind me of what a great image can come out of this camera.  Thanks for doing such a great job on this photo and inspiring me to keep trying for shots like this just when I was starting to get down on myself and my camera.  Great job!', '2005-07-19 13:04:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1546760, 201459, 12311, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GeneralE:</b></div><hr/><i> I"m especially interested in seeing how the shot in portrait orientation came out, and how many frames you shot off between you all that day : )<br/>Nice repeating composition with the flagpoles. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Paul, the portrait shot of the little guy (in blue) came out just fine.  Problem is, he just got the white flag and completely missed the fort.  Doh!  ;-).  Must have been 100+ frames among us (gotta love digital and those compact flash disks!)</td>', 'Originally posted by GeneralE: I"m especially interested in seeing how the shot in portrait orientation came out, and how many frames you shot off between you all that day : )Nice repeating composition with the flagpoles.  Paul, the portrait shot of the little guy (in blue) came out just fine.  Problem is, he just got the white flag and completely missed the fort.  Doh!  ;-).  Must have been 100+ frames among us (gotta love digital and those compact flash disks!)', '2005-07-19 15:25:43.000000', NULL, 0);
